<!-- HERO -->
<header class="post-hero">
  <div class="tags">
    <span class="tag tag-purple">Sequence Models</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">Long Context</span>
    <span class="tag tag-green">Interactive</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Memory Caching: RNNs with Growing Memory</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    RNNs forget. Transformers remember everything but cost O(L²). Memory Caching threads the needle:
    cache the RNN's compressed hidden state at segment boundaries, let every future token attend to
    those checkpoints, and scale from O(L) all the way toward O(L²) by choosing how many segments to keep.
    Titans + MC closes the recall gap with Transformers on Needle-in-a-Haystack while staying subquadratic.
  </p>
  <div class="post-hero-meta">
