<p>
  The commonsense reasoning results (average over PIQA, HellaSwag, WinoGrande, ARC-e, ARC-c, SIQA,
  BoolQ) at 1.3B / 100B tokens show a consistent ladder: Transformer++ 49.64 → base Titans 56.82
  → Titans + GRM <strong>58.33</strong>. MC adds +1.5 points over the already-strong Titans base.
</p>

<h3>LongBench and retrieval tasks</h3>
<p>
  On LongBench (14 long-document tasks), DLA + GRM achieves an average of 30.51 → 38.03 vs its
  base, a gain of nearly 8 points. On in-context retrieval (SWDE, SQuAD, TriviaQA, DROP, FDA, NQ),
  DLA + GRM scores 40.50 vs DLA base 30.51, again the GRM variant leading all MC variants.
</p>

<h3>Throughput</h3>
<p>
  SSC has the best efficiency profile: at long context lengths it matches base-RNN throughput while
  delivering near-GRM recall. All MC variants significantly outperform Transformers in tokens/second
  at 8K+ context — the compute advantage of subquadratic architecture is preserved, with recall
  now strongly competitive.
</p>

